  "notes": "יוטיקט (youticket.co.il) — WordPress + The Events Calendar; a white-label storefront of the Cartis/Kartisim ticketing back-end (website = you.kartisim.co.il/announce/buy/<id>, images from bravo.israelinfo.co.il — the same catalogue kupatbravo.co.il fronts). TEC REST /wp-json/tribe/events/v1/events, 50 per page, next_rest_url pagination (~34 pages ≈ 1,700 upcoming performances, ~14 s / 2 MB per page → ~8 min per run, hence 48 h). Fields: title (HTML-entity encoded, decoded at save), local start/end_date, venue.venue/city/address (city filled on every row; Hebrew → city_aliases), cost '109₪ – 129₪' → first number, categories → raw_categories, excerpt → description, website = the outbound buy link (purchase_link). No performer field → artist_name empty. Overlap measured 2026-09-20 on the first 50 rows: 24 announce ids already exist as kupatbravo source_ids and 41/50 (name,date) pairs were already in prod (bravo 26, mevalim 26) — the marginal ~20 % are Bravo performances kupatbravo's 7 first-pages miss; cross-source dedup is the weekly (venue,date,name≈) job. name = the quoted show title only (the TEC title appends ' – <category> ב<city>' boilerplate; the regex keeps the text inside the leading &quot;…&quot;). Dry run 2026-09-20 (6 pages): 300 events, venue/city/price/image ≈100 %; 185/300 already in prod (mevalim 123, bravo 91)."
